{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Test</b> — an expression of entreaty, like: \"I pray you, entreat the face of YHWH.\"" "<b>And the meaning of \"ten days\"</b> — for no living creature can endure the bad [food] except nine days; so the naturalists have mentioned. And \"instead of the king's food, give us seeds\" — they are legumes, as they age. And instead of wine, give us water:"], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:53.245129604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}